[34.009437, "o", "62:\t exec/4, shell/2, subsystem/4, send/3, send/4, send/5, \r\n150:              exec_ch_msg/0\r\n169:                      | exec_ch_msg()\r\n218:A remote execution can terminate violently because of a signal. Then this\r\n319:This message requests that the server starts execution of the given command.\r\n320:This event is sent as a result of calling [ssh_connection:exec/4 ](`exec/4`).\r\n324:-type exec_ch_msg() :: {exec,\r\n343:%% remote execution of a program. The program may be a shell, an\r\n393:%% execution of the given command. \r\n397:executing the given command. The result is several messages according to the\r\n398:following pattern. The last message is a channel close message, as the `exec`\r\n399:request is a one-time execution that closes the channel when it is done.\r\n401:- **N x [data message(s)](`t:data_ch_msg/0`)** - The result of executing the\r\n415:  `ssh_client_channel` started for the execution of the command has now been\r\n419:[One-Time Execution](using_ssh.md#one-time-execution) for examples.\r\n421:-spec exec(ConnectionRef, ChannelId, Command, Timeout) -> result() when\r\n427:exec(ConnectionRef, ChannelId, Command, TimeOut) ->\r\n428:    ssh_connection_handler:request(ConnectionRef, self(), ChannelId, \"exec\",\r\n438:shell (typically defined in /etc/passwd in Unix systems) is executed at the\r\n458:Is to be called by a client-channel process for requesting to execute a\r\n"]
[34.009544, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@5252d2d4dfad:/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src# "]
